WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.366
Amazon Warehousing and Distribution, or AWD, is a low-cost bulk storage solution for your inventory

00:00:07.366 --> 00:00:14.271
that distributes to the Amazon Store and other distribution channels, saving you time and money

00:00:14.271 --> 00:00:19.336
when you have large quantities of inventory to store and distribute.

00:00:19.336 --> 00:00:24.860
Utilizing AWD for your bulk storage can help you reduce storage costs.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:31.590
By sending your inventory in bulk to AWD facilities, you can take advantage of lower per unit storage

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.460
fees compared to standard FBA.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.378
Automate Replenishment.

00:00:35.378 --> 00:00:41.640
AWD automatically replenishes and optimizes your inventory in FBA fulfillment centers.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.628
Expand your distribution.

00:00:43.628 --> 00:00:50.475
Your inventory stored in AWD facilities can be distributed to the Amazon Store as well as other

00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:51.280
sales channels.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:58.446
Plus, AWD pricing covers FBA inbound placement fees, making AWD a simplified, cost-effective way

00:00:58.446 --> 00:01:02.054
to store and distribute your inventory with Amazon

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:04.760
handling the logistics on your behalf.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.600
The Amazon Warehousing and Distribution Program supports a variety of FBA products.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.842
When you book shipments, Amazon will validate that the ASINs you're attempting to send

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.500
are eligible.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.140
Eligible SKUs must meet the following criteria.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:28.312
Conveyable inventory with maximum carton box dimensions of 25 by 25 by 25 inches and maximum weight

00:01:28.312 --> 00:01:29.620
of 50 pounds.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:37.476
Individual SKUs inside a carton box cannot be larger than 18 by 14 by 8 inches or weigh more than

00:01:37.476 --> 00:01:38.180
20 pounds.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.660
Cartons boxes must contain one unique SKU each, not a mix of SKUs.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:49.100
Certain product categories may also require pre-approval from Amazon before listing.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:56.515
Review the Amazon Warehousing and Distribution AWD Product Eligibility Help Page to check for specific

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:57.480
product eligibility.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:05.213
To start using the Amazon Warehousing and Distribution Program, in Seller Central, go to the Inventory

00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:06.506
drop-down menu

00:02:06.506 --> 00:02:09.178
and select Warehousing and Distribution AWD.

00:02:09.178 --> 00:02:12.800
From the Program Page, click Send to AWD.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.175
Within two to three days of creating your first AWD shipment,

00:02:17.175 --> 00:02:23.300
you will be able to access the AWD Inventory page to manage your shipments.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.520
There are no fees to get started.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.120
You'll only be charged when you ship your inventory to our facilities.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:36.520
Remember, the Warehousing and Distribution tools are only visible to users with permissions.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:42.352
If you don't have permissions, ask your primary account holder to grant them to you via the User

00:02:42.352 --> 00:02:43.000
Permissions page.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.993
By leveraging AWD, you can streamline your inventory management,

00:02:47.993 --> 00:02:53.540
reduce storage costs, and expand the distribution of your products.
